877 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 360 0 R
/E (Escrow: The buyer typically places an earnest money deposit into an escrow account as a sign of good faith  until the transaction is completed. If the buyer backs out of the sale for a reason not specified in the contract, the seller is typically entitled to keep the escrow money.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
878 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 360 0 R
/E (Contingencies: A contingency is when there's something that the buyer or seller needs to do for the transaction to go forward. The buyer conducts inspections, appraisals, and any other necessary investigations to ensure the property's condition and value align with their expectations.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
879 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 360 0 R
/E (Loan Approval and Appraisal: The buyer's lender evaluates the property's value to determine if the buyer qualifies for a mortgage. An appraisal ensures the property's value matches or exceeds the agreed-upon purchase price. Depending on the contract, meeting these approvals may be contingencies of the sale.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
